## Why Leiby

I started Leiby because the best work I've done happened when I stopped acting like a supplier and started acting like part of the team. When your problem becomes my problem, the questions get sharper and the answers get simpler.

## Design and build, under one roof

I studied computer science before I moved into design, and I still build a lot of what I design. That means fewer surprises between the mockup and the live product, and decisions that are made with real constraints in mind.

## How I like to work

- Start with users and data, not opinions.
- Keep the team close: short loops, shared files, honest trade-offs.
- Ship early, measure, then improve.
